摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Enhanced ACP (Agent Client Protocol) server for DeepSeek Harness (dsh) — drop-in bridge for the Zed editor: block-level streaming, usage/stat telemetry, model & reasoning-effort switching, permission presets, session resume & archive. Install: dsh plugin add","id":"gh:1333657529","install_available":true,"language":"JavaScript","name":"dsh-acp-enhanced","slug":"grunmin/dsh-acp-enhanced","topics":["acp","agent-client-protocol","ai-agent","deepseek-harness","dsh","dsh-plugin","llm","zed","zed-editor"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Enhanced ACP (Agent Client Protocol) server for DeepSeek Harness (dsh) — drop-in bridge for the Zed "},{"id":"p1s2","text":"editor: block-level streaming, usage/stat telemetry, model & reasoning-effort switching, permission "},{"id":"p1s3","text":"presets, session resume & archive. Install: dsh plugin add"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"**中文 | English** · Changelog"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"# dsh-acp-enhanced"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"An enhanced Agent Client Protocol (ACP) server for\nDeepSeek Harness (dsh), built for ACP\neditors lik"},{"id":"p4s2","text":"e **Zed**. It is a drop-in replacement for the official `@deepseek-ai/dsh-acp`\nbridge: the official "},{"id":"p4s3","text":"bridge only streams plain text, this one exposes the Web GUI's\ncapabilities — streaming, telemetry, "},{"id":"p4s4","text":"model/permission control, session management, MCP —\nover the ACP wire."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"## Features"},{"id":"p6s1","text":"### Output & telemetry"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"- **Token-level streaming, on by default**: the reply and the model's thinking reach the\neditor whil"},{"id":"p7s2","text":"e it is still writing (`agent_message_chunk` / `agent_thought_chunk`,\ncoalesced on a 75 ms timer). T"},{"id":"p7s3","text":"he one cost of sending text before its block commits is\nthat a mid-block retry cannot take its aband"},{"id":"p7s4","text":"oned partial back: a visible\n`_[stream interrupted — retrying]_` marker separates it from the retrie"},{"id":"p7s5","text":"d attempt. Set\n`streamDeltas: false` on the acp-enhanced row (`DSH_ACP_STREAM_DELTAS=false`) for the"},{"id":"p7s6","text":"\nolder block-granularity behaviour, where cancelled/retried attempts never leak torn\noutput at all b"},{"id":"p7s7","text":"ut nothing renders until the block commits\n- **Full telemetry**: context usage ring plus cache hit r"},{"id":"p7s8","text":"ate / TPS / input-output-reasoning\ntokens / tool timing / turn counts (`usage_update._meta` carries "},{"id":"p7s9","text":"the full breakdown). The\nring's denominator is the routed model's declared `contextWindow`, folded f"},{"id":"p7s10","text":"rom the session\nlog so a resumed thread keeps it (the harness logs `request/context` once and does n"},{"id":"p7s11","text":"ot\nre-emit it for an unchanged route). dsh's own `dsh-compaction-basic` row auto-compacts at\n~80% of"},{"id":"p7s12","text":" that window and is mounted by the `standard`/`ptc`/`cordis` presets (never\n`minimal`); `/compact` f"},{"id":"p7s13","text":"orces it manually. A route whose adapter declares no `contextWindow` has no denominator,\nso the ring"},{"id":"p7s14","text":" reports `used === size`.\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"## Compatibility"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"One bridge binary, one declared harness surface: **dsh ≥ 0.1.6-alpha.1** (peer range\n`^0.1.6-alpha.1"},{"id":"p9s2","text":" || ^0.1.7-alpha.1 || ^0.2.0-rc.2 || ^0.2.1-rc.2`). All four lines in that range\nare **boot-verified"},{"id":"p9s3","text":"** — handshake, profile settle and a real `session/new` — on every CI run,\nplus a cross-generation l"},{"id":"p9s4","text":"ink check and a `scripts/support-claim-test.mjs` guard that pins this\nparagraph's claim against npm'"},{"id":"p9s5","text":"s own semver. The bridge consumes only the harness's **declared**\nsurface: services in `docs/capabil"},{"id":"p9s6","text":"ity-seams.md`, events in\n`docs/event-producer-consumer.md`, published package exports. `scripts/api-"},{"id":"p9s7","text":"surface-check.mjs`\nfails on anything else (a blocking CI step). There is no feature sniffing and no "},{"id":"p9s8","text":"generation\nmatrix: 0.1.7 needed exactly two adaptations — a **member probe**\n(`presets.resolveMounta"},{"id":"p9s9","text":"ble`, private through 0.1.6 and gone in 0.1.7, replaced there by\n`resolve()` plus the row's own `bro"},{"id":"p9s10","text":"ken` verdict) and a **generation-gated row** in\n`cordis.patch.yml` for the repackaged agent-preset r"},{"id":"p9s11","text":"oster, which reads the booting\ninstallation's own manifest version (below); 0.2.0 needed **none** (e"},{"id":"p9s12","text":"very package the bridge\nimports changed only by version, and its one new export is additive), and 0."},{"id":"p9s13","text":"2.1 needs **none\neither** — it is the first line whose range alternative narrows nothing (see below)"},{"id":"p9s14","text":". A host\nwithout either\nfalls back to the older shape; neither path can fail a boot."},{"id":"p10s1","text":"The one thing that does fail silently is the **host's own peer gate**: from 0.1.7\n`@deepseek-ai/dsh-"},{"id":"p10s2","text":"app-boot` checks every bundle's declared `@deepseek-ai/dsh*` peers against\nthe running CLI version a"},{"id":"p10s3","text":"nd, when they do not match, drops that bundle's whole patch layer with\na single stderr line (`dsh: s"},{"id":"p10s4","text":"kipping profile bundle \"…\"`). A range that stops one line short is\ntherefore not a warning but a mis"},{"id":"p10s5","text":"sing bridge — which is why the range above is both declared\n*and* booted per line. The install path "},{"id":"p10s6","text":"is stricter still: from 0.1.7 the plugin manager also\nresolves **every row `name` in the bundle's pa"},{"id":"p10s7","text":"tch files** and runs the same gate on each package,\nrejecting the whole installation (`incompatible-"},{"id":"p10s8","text":"version`) when one disagrees — even a row that the\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"## Known limitations"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"Audio attachments are not supported (audio capability is not advertised), text streams\ntoken-by-toke"},{"id":"p12s2","text":"n by default (`streamDeltas: false` restores block buffering, see\nFeatures), one in-flight prompt pe"},{"id":"p12s3","text":"r session. MCP supports stdio and streamable HTTP\n(legacy SSE / `acp` transports are not advertised)"},{"id":"p12s4","text":".\n`session/fork` / `session/resume` are not implemented (capabilities\nundeclared, compliant clients "},{"id":"p12s5","text":"will not call them). `session/delete` is not advertised\neither: the harness declares no public persi"},{"id":"p12s6","text":"stence delete, so persisted sessions are\nnever removed by the bridge (see Compatibility)."},{"id":"p13s1","text":"Multi-root workspaces are advertised and all roots are visible to the model, but dsh's\nsandbox polic"},{"id":"p13s2","text":"y resolves **one writable root per session** (the primary `cwd`, i.e.\n`session.header.cwd`) and the "},{"id":"p13s3","text":"local sandboxes bind exactly that root for writes. Reads\nwork in every root; under `workspace-write`"},{"id":"p13s4","text":" a write under an additional root is denied\nfirst and needs escalation/approval, while `danger-full-"},{"id":"p13s5","text":"access` writes everywhere.\nTrue multi-root write enforcement belongs in dsh core (`dsh-sandbox-polic"},{"id":"p13s6","text":"y` /\n`dsh-sandbox-local` would need a root list instead of a single root)."},{"id":"p14s1","text":"Agent presets take over the model-facing rows: the shipped `cordis.patch.yml` disables\nthe dsh-base "},{"id":"p14s2","text":"rows a preset owns (tool-bash/fs/subagent/todo/web/… — exactly the official\ndsh-web-app/tui list min"},{"id":"p14s3","text":"us `hmr`, kept version-agnostic across generations: a row a given\ngeneration does not ship is warned"},{"id":"p14s4","text":" and skipped by the patch applier) and mounts the\n`agent-presets` roster (`standard`\ndefault; `ptc`/"},{"id":"p14s5","text":"`minimal`/`cordis` ship with the dsh CLI; your own presets are declared as\n`@deepseek-ai/dsh-agent-p"},{"id":"p14s6","text":"reset` rows from 0.1.7 on — see\nYour own presets). The bundle's own patch applies\nautomatically (pac"},{"id":"p14s7","text":"kage.json `dsh.bundle.patch`) — do **not** copy it into the profile's\nuser-layer `cordis.patch.yml`,"},{"id":"p14s8","text":" or the loader rejects the duplicate entry ids at boot.\nWhen **upgrading** a profile that already ca"},{"id":"p14s9","text":"rries a customized user-layer patch, keep\nonly your custom row configs there (e.g. `includeAllProvid"},{"id":"p14s10","text":"ers: true` on the\n[该节后续省略]"}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
